  "findings": [
    "Stage 56 records ramoops return within arm_init; it does not prove BSD or a CDC worker was reached.",
    "The actual native file has no boot_progress functions, and the retained target compile record disables XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS; boot_progress_stage expands to a no-op.",
    "The actual packaged ADT contains a defaults node but no serial-device and no consistent-debug-root property. The known boot arguments contain neither serial-device nor serial-device-name.",
    "Pinned PE_consistent_debug_inherit returns -1 without consistent-debug-root. Pinned serial_init returns 0 when no serial device is selected, before driver setup. No current evidence identifies either call as a blocking cause.",
    "The CDC entry occurs in bsd_init after IOKitInitializeTime; the worker uses scheduling and timer deadlines and must not be moved into arm_init unchanged.",
    "All live clock/PHY/role/SMMU refusals are printf-only. Current device feedback contains none of those register values, so no guard failure is established.",
    "The current reporter uses global stack, mutable tables and temporary TTBR0/TCR mappings. Do not call it from a scheduled CDC worker or concurrently from CPUs.",
    "A future read-only ring-tail snapshot can use verified static symbol bounds, stable index/lock checks and bounded sanitized bytes; it must report dropped_bytes, because this ring drops new bytes when full. Pre-scheduler snapshots cannot contain future CDC worker outcomes."
  ],
